  "interpretation_limits": [
    "072C learned_sequence trains position only; its speed/course equal ordinary Mean. These are not trained Transformer speed/course predictions, so PTFM speed/course superiority does not establish superiority over a comparable learned three-state competitor.",
    "Speed improvement appears in all 300 scenes and all 38 components; heading MAE improves in 282 scenes and 31 components. This is broad development-set evidence, not independent identities or multiple-seed evidence.",
    "Near-equal speed MAE with and without a supported helper does not prove helpers have no value; populations differ. Conversely, large overall speed improvement alone does not establish a multisource-fusion contribution. Training-only constant/prior and anchor-only supervised controls remain necessary.",
    "Position, speed and heading use 442263, 442476 and 442000 valid points respectively. The receipt stratification table displays position counts; those cannot be reused as speed/course denominators. Helper-availability query counts include rows without valid attribute truth.",
    "Position MAE is worse in 297/300 scenes and 38/38 components, but not every tail metric or subset is worse: P99 beats Anchor and aggregate RMSE outside the largest component beats 072C.",
    "Reported exposure matches 072C, but architecture, initialization, output attributes and objectives differ. This is a task adaptation comparison, not a backbone-only ablation or author reproduction. 4000 updates do not establish adequate convergence.",
    "Training source speed normalizer mean 55.47 and standard deviation 196.83 are input statistics, not truth statistics; native speed unit and possible prior/shrinkage mechanisms require direct truth/prediction analysis before physical or causal interpretation."
  ]
